      "side": 1,
      "message": "It was the original idea to make objmgr method (etAssociatedSubTreePathsById) to reduce 2 dbus calls into 1 dbus call.\n\nSo, instead 2 steps of dbus calls ( getValidFabricAdapterPath, and getAssociatedSubTreePaths), should `objmgr` be the one to change `getAssociatedSubTreePathsById()` to return the error if `adapterId` is not found?\n\nFrom that view, it seems the issue is at objmgr which does not handle the case `Id` not found.",
      "revId": "ef3e627045904ce866e3411fc2d977bc7fc15d23",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6a4b73f_fcfdd0de",
        "filename": "redfish-core/lib/fabric_ports.hpp",
